Mechanism:
- crates/bboxy450-term/src/launcher.rs — Controller owns the existing native
  Launcher record. Query changes, wrapping selection, hover, explicit/typed
  descent, climb, Escape, reroll intents, Enter/click/digits use view()/activation().
  No new item tree, matching implementation, provider model, IO or winit.
- Activate returns the selected id and original modifiers to the caller; it
  never spawns or sends. enter_picks parents pick on Enter, while Right opens
  children. Both parent default picks and leaf picks respect the cap;
  navigation stays available. Down/link-disabled rows refuse activation.
- replace_items keeps the selected id across catalog reordering and truncates
  a path whose host/parent vanished or no longer exposes children. Provider
  inputs in the tests come from Model.provider_launcher_items(), not a second
  provider model. Connecting remains browseable per the existing projection;
  the backend's Connected/Degraded spawn fence is deliberately unchanged.
- crates/bboxy450-term/src/lib.rs exports the pure module; tests/launcher.rs has
  15 synthetic controller cases. Text-field editing, name generation and
  bounded dispatch are caller responsibilities expressed as pure outcomes.
- crates/bbt-ui/src/modules/launcher.rs:25 carries serde-default enter_picks,
  renamed enterPicks, and tests/launchers.rs tests true/missing/default children.
- crates/bboxybook/capture-inputs.js:342 preserves that public constructor flag
  through capture. Matching, materials, geometry and drawing do not read it.
  Wren fixed the source lab cap bypass in 8ae27d9 before this branch froze.

